From: dagu <dagu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: venus: stub missing ICC paths on dagu

dagu cannot enable CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SM8250: the BCM voter
rpmh_write_batch() times out on this QHEE chain. Without a provider,
devm_of_icc_get("video-mem") / ("cpu-cfg") returns -EPROBE_DEFER and
qcom-venus never leaves probe.

Treat a missing path as optional. icc_set_bw(NULL, ...) in
drivers/interconnect/core.c is a documented no-op, and pm_helpers.c
load_scale_bw() only calls icc_set_bw() on the already-fetched
video_path — no extra get() lives there.

The board DTS also deletes interconnects / interconnect-names so
of_icc_get() returns NULL before this branch; the stub is the
belt if those properties come back.

Do not enable INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SM8250 to "fix" this.

Signed-off-by: dagu <dagu@localhost>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -390,13 +390,23 @@ static int venus_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(core->base))
 		return PTR_ERR(core->base);
 
 	core->video_path = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "video-mem");
-	if (IS_ERR(core->video_path))
-		return PTR_ERR(core->video_path);
+	if (IS_ERR(core->video_path)) {
+		/* dagu: ICC video-mem stubbed — no SM8250 ICC provider.
+		 * icc_set_bw(NULL) is a no-op. Do not EPROBE_DEFER.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(dev, "ICC video-mem stubbed, ignoring bandwidth voting\n");
+		core->video_path = NULL;
+	}
 
 	core->cpucfg_path = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "cpu-cfg");
-	if (IS_ERR(core->cpucfg_path))
-		return PTR_ERR(core->cpucfg_path);
+	if (IS_ERR(core->cpucfg_path)) {
+		/* dagu: ICC cpu-cfg stubbed */
+		dev_warn(dev, "ICC cpu-cfg stubbed, ignoring bandwidth voting\n");
+		core->cpucfg_path = NULL;
+	}
 
 	core->irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
 	if (core->irq < 0)
 		return core->irq;
